WEBVTT

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.920
Kazahamaurara Women's Academy Entrance Examinations

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.410
Hello? This is Morikawa.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:21.450
This is Shinozuka.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.610
I apologize for calling this early in the morning.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.140
It's okay, I was just about to get ready.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:27.150
What's going on?

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.550
Perhaps this could've waited until I came to pick you up, but...

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:31.860
What's wrong? Did something happen?

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.010
The Venus Festival. It's been finalized.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.630
Congratulations, Yuki-san.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:41.810
Yuki-san?

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.660
nemuri nasai ima wa tada

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.660
Sleep, for now

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:57.570
watashi no naka de doko ni mo ikanai de

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:57.570
Inside of me, and don't go anywhere

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:18.580
madoromi no fuchi de yureteru gunjou iro no yo

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:18.580
Through the slumbering ultramarine sky

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:24.100
majiwaru koto no nai hoshi wo sagashiteru

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:24.100
I am searching for stars that will never cross

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:31.800
anata wo motomeru yubisaki yami ni samayotte

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:31.800
These fingertips search for you, but are lost in darkness

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:40.680
mogaite mo nukedesenai ai no umi ni oboreteku

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:40.680
I try but I can't escape, and I drown in the sea of love

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:48.570
yawaranai toiki ni kokoro sae mo furueru

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:48.570
Your tender sigh makes my heart tremble

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:54.190
karamaru utsukushi kumo no ito no you

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:54.190
Seemingly entangled in the beautiful strands of a spider web

00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:58.680
ugokenai no watashi wo yurushite

00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:58.680
I cannot move, please forgive me

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.010
anata no ude ni dakarete nemuru

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.010
I am sleeping with your arms around me

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:05.230
nani mo kamo sutetatte ii

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:05.230
I don't mind losing anything else

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:12.760
ii kono mama no maboroshi nante zukuru no wa yamete

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:12.760
Stop pretending that you are a good girl

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.220
hontou no watashi wo mitsukete

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.220
Find the real me

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:22.300
zutto matteru

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:22.300
I'll be waiting forever

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:37.490
You don't look very happy.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:40.150
No, that's not it-

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:43.330
You seem to have had something on your mind for a while, now.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.230
Do you know who the entrant is for M3?

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.140
It's Matsuyama Menou-san.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:53.360
How come...

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:58.380
Page 23
Hoping to be nursed by her and eat her 
homecooked food, he wanted to catch a cold.
The suffering that was to come 
never even occured to him.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.530
Well? Are you backing out?

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:15.800
No.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:22.590
I... promised.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:24.010
Right.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.930
Then let's use your new song for the Venus Festival.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:28.520
Then...

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:29.770
You won't be needing this.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:34.650
Start by singing to your own accompaniment.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:43.910
That's right.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.300
That's right?

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.450
Well, that's what the President said.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:49.430
... I see.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:52.580
But... yes, it's been decided.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:57.730
Please stop the car.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:58.750
Eh, uhh...

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:03.840
Are you fine with taking the rest of the day off?

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.010
I'm fine with it, but...

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:26.660
Where's Touya-kun?

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:28.610
Taking the day off.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:31.420
So you came here to check up on me?

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:33.090
You must be bored.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:35.260
I heard they decided who's going to the Venus Festival.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:38.040
Looks like it, though it's going to be such a chore.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.420
Isn't it in your best interest to back out?

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.890
And you're going to go instead of me?

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:49.400
That's what you came here to say?

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:53.420
Ahh, so the great Ogata Rina's really fallen from grace, hasn't she?

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:55.620
What are you going to do if word gets out?

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.740
So, you know already...

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:04.930
Ever since you came here, I knew I was in trouble.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:09.530
That woman, she didn't really care about this at all,

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.330
and so she completely pulled out.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:15.560
I thought about ending all of this, but...

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.230
I was worried...

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.150
It's about time we finish up,

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:27.110
since it'll still be bad no matter how many times we fix it.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:28.870
Menou-san.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.600
Shall we talk for a little while?

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.260
All right, please stop.

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:00.160
Misaki-san?

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:09.010
So it's a job. Isn't that great?

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:11.010
It's nothing big.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:12.860
I won't be credited for it, anyway.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:16.300
Tamaru-kun contacted me...

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:17.770
Tamaru did?

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:18.690
Did something happen?

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:21.560
No, nothing important...

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:22.780
That's not good.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:24.510
It's fine.

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.610
I prepared myself for the worst,

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:29.540
but thanks to a certain someone, everything went fine.

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:31.310
I have a job now, too.

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:34.890
But, I don't know how things will turn out...

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:36.630
Fujii-kun, you're the same way, right?

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:37.550
Since Yuki is...

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:40.270
What do you want to say?

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:40.270
What do you want to say?

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:45.390
Say it again.

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:48.310
I'm thinking of breaking up with Nanase-kun.

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:49.340
Don't make me say it again.

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:51.720
Break up? But why?

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:52.730
Did you two have a fight?

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:55.390
Then why?

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:56.770
Tell me the reason why.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:58.690
There is no reason.

00:06:58.690 --> 00:06:59.850
If that's the case...

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.740
But, weren't the two of you getting along?

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:04.300
You saw us?

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:07.500
How much do you know about us?

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:10.320
Misaki-san...

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:18.240
Horrible.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.640
Men are horrible.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:23.100
They're naïve, and selfish,

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:26.070
and they don't understand a thing about a woman's feelings.

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:28.940
What are you saying? Akira's not that kind of person-

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:30.410
Women are even worse.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:32.030
Myself included.

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:33.390
I'll end up just the same.

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:36.190
You don't like Akira anymore?

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:38.190
That's not it.

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.940
Didn't I already tell you? There's no reason.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:45.620
Actually, there's one reason...

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:46.580
And it's this.

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:05.290
It's strange, isn't it?

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:06.460
It's pathetic.

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:09.540
But please don't laugh.

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:11.940
I don't want you to hate Touya.

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:20.550
That's how he tries his best to fight.

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:24.080
I have something to ask of you.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:26.400
Could you praise Touya for me?

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:28.770
Tell him he did great.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.770
Tell him he was cool.

00:08:32.350 --> 00:08:33.570
Wait.

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:34.990
Wait!

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:37.440
Say to Touya...

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:39.120
Tell Touya...

00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:46.290
Yuki...

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:02.080
Kazahamaurara Women's Academy - Acceptance List

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:18.560
Uncle,

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:20.060
Just as how memories

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:21.810
cannot be erased,

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:23.310
As well as how I cannot abandon

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:25.110
these feelings for someone,

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:26.570
As I hold these feelings in my heart,

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:28.320
and there is nothing left to do but retreat,

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:30.110
I've finally realized.

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:32.070
As time cools any passion I may have,

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:33.570
there is nothing I can do but

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:33.570
wait somewhere far away.

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:35.330
The me that now

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:36.830
stands in front of your son

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:39.370
is but an empty shell of a body.

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:41.150
Please don't worry,

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:41.150
and

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:41.150
rest in peace, forever.

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:45.960
-Misaki Sawakura

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:19.260
Tomorrow... how sudden.

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:20.710
My uncle...

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:24.010
Uh, my dad's older brother can't leave work,

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:26.120
so the only day he can come is tomorrow.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:28.520
The arrangements are pretty much done.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:32.050
We'll load the stuff in the car, and clean up after that.

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:34.680
Your dad made things easy for you, didn't he?

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:37.600
He just wanted to go back to where I'm not around as soon as possible.

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:39.010
Oh, you...

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:43.120
Sorry, I can't help you.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:44.310
All right.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:47.400
Ah, I can't expect Haruka to help either.

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:49.480
Looks like it'll just be me and Misaki-san-

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:54.860
Clearly the word "delicacy" isn't in your vocabulary.

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:56.130
Sorry, my bad.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:01.830
There's something I've always wanted to try.

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:03.590
Mind if I do it now?

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:05.440
Sure, what is it?

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:07.900
A hammer for he who squanders savior-goddesses.

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:10.270
Squander? Hammer?

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:12.440
Akira, you're using complicated expressions again.

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:15.110
Yeah, clench your teeth, Touya.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:29.990
Now all that's left is cleaning up.

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:30.570
Yeah.

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:32.630
Ow- ouch...

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:35.340
Are you okay? It looks painful.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:40.230
Weird, I had no idea it was possible to get cold sores there.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:42.280
Don't you normally get them on the lips?

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:45.210
Should I tell her what really happened?

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:50.640
A long time ago... or should I say until I was in middle school,

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:52.780
our relatives who were attending university,

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:54.610
or the families of my father's acquaintances,

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:57.770
they would live here as if they were boarders.

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:00.820
They would play with me often.

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:04.810
I'd borrow things like books and records.

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:06.720
It's very well-cleaned.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:10.160
This place used to have so much energy.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:11.840
What a waste, isn't it?

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:14.960
It's too large for me to live in by myself.

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:16.900
It'll be fine for two people, right?

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:17.920
You could rent out the room.

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:31.040
I heard Yuki would always visit your father whenever she had time.

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:31.820
Eh?

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:34.040
Ah, seems so.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:36.850
It put your dad at ease, don't you think?

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:40.120
It probably made him nervous.

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:41.400
You know, my dad's actually-

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:43.360
Did you manage to talk to him?

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:48.790
I'm sorry...

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:50.790
Misaki-san...

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:53.680
Just one last time, just for today...

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:56.250
I'd like you to fall in love with me.

00:12:58.280 --> 00:13:00.530
Just for today, okay?

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:08.640
O-Ouch...

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:10.070
Sorry.

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:15.000
Farewell, Misaki-san

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:31.070
It's Mizuki.

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:34.160
I know this comes late, but I passed the exam.

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:37.570
It's not like I want you to say anything about it, though...

00:13:37.570 --> 00:13:38.900
That's all.

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:48.560
It makes me mad that Aesop's actually Yuki's boyfriend.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:50.880
You want to say that we don't match, right?

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:53.390
No, you do match.

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:56.250
You match so much, you're like siblings.

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:57.990
And that's what makes me mad.

00:13:57.990 --> 00:13:59.000
I'm honored.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:02.040
Plus, don't take this the wrong way,

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:05.420
but the only reason I called you was so I could give you this chocolate.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:09.640
It has nothing to do with whether I got accepted or not.

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:11.090
You've said that plenty of times.

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:14.270
So about treating this whole thing as a celebration for my getting accepted,

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:16.180
I'd like you to stop it.

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:18.690
I'm not a kid anymore.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:20.860
I won't.

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:25.520
Like going shopping and having dinner, you don't have to...

00:14:25.520 --> 00:14:27.020
You don't want dinner?

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:28.440
I do, but...

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:33.610
There's one thing I want you to say to me, no matter what.

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:36.010
Praise me, tell me I did great.

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:41.340
Well done! Really, you worked hard!

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:43.340
Congratulations, Mana-chan!

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:45.730
This is so embarrassing, let go!

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:49.000
I can't, my hands are frozen from the cold and I can't move them.

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:52.440
You really... are an idiot...

00:14:58.660 --> 00:14:59.960
Haruka.

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:01.320
You coming in?

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:06.670
Here, one-day-late obligatory chocolate.

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:07.880
Thank you.

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:09.650
Here, in return.

00:15:09.650 --> 00:15:10.370
Already?

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:12.680
Yep, doubling as a White Day gift.

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:16.990
Oh right, it's my birthday today.

00:15:16.990 --> 00:15:17.940
Geez.

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:20.020
What is it? Shoes?

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:24.160
Yep, sneakers. The pair in the display window.

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:25.320
You saw them, didn't you?

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:29.450
I was thinking of getting something tennis-related,

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:31.680
but since I have terrible taste...

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:32.890
You're not happy?

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:33.650
I'm neutral.

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:35.650
Right, great.

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:39.690
Haruka, is it okay?

00:15:41.630 --> 00:15:43.510
Yeah, they're just right.

00:15:43.510 --> 00:15:45.070
I wasn't talking about the shoes.

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:46.750
Then what?

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:47.960
I mean...

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:52.070
Yeah, I'm fine. My mind's clear now.

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:53.190
I see...

00:15:53.710 --> 00:15:56.200
You don't belong to me.

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:57.100
I'll give you back to Yuki.

00:15:57.730 --> 00:15:58.680
You know-

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:00.600
My seat is here, it seems.

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:04.180
You can be just my brother, after all.

00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:05.770
You...

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.570
What's wrong? Are you crying?

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:13.350
No, it's just kind of bright out.

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:14.880
It's cloudy, though...

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:22.950
A date.

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:25.640
It's called a sightseeing trip, but you wouldn't know about it.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:28.210
That's an old bike of mine.

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:29.800
Let's go.

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:32.660
Ah, again...

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:33.790
See you later, Touya.

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:36.280
Yeah, take care.

00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:41.950
I didn't know he could ride a bike.

00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:52.070
Oh?

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:57.420
You're working hard.

00:16:57.420 --> 00:16:58.550
I have nothing else to do.

00:16:58.550 --> 00:16:59.450
Are you giving me attitude?

00:17:00.970 --> 00:17:03.030
Where's Menou?

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:04.440
She left earlier in the evening.

00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:07.340
And where's Fujii-kun?

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:10.520
He's on a break until he calms down.

00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:11.440
Right.

00:17:13.610 --> 00:17:14.880
President?

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:17.370
Have you seen Ei-chan recently?

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:18.270
No...

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:27.920
You know Misumi, one of my employees?

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:32.180
According to him, in the basement of that café Ei-chan hides out at, what's it called,

00:17:32.180 --> 00:17:35.850
your brother hides paintings that would be worth
hundreds of millions of yen if they were authentic.

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:39.950
He didn't say a word about it to me,

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:43.080
though he was bragging about it to Menou's manager.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:47.560
It's not a hideout if everyone knows about it, right?

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:49.760
I heard he offered to dispose of the paintings,

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:52.970
saying that there were counterfeits among them.

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:56.550
I don't know a thing about paintings,

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.520
but do you think Ei-chan will be fine?

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:02.160
He'll be fine, if Nagase-san's with him.

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:06.270
Ah, he's the owner of the café.

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:08.960
He's also a Daddy Longlegs of sorts to both me and my brother.

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:14.570
From a talent production company, you say?

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:17.170
They asked me if I would buy some paintings.

00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:20.730
Their origins are suspicious, so they may be counterfeits.

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:22.980
But, if they're actually authentic...

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:24.540
... it would be profitable?

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:28.190
Ten paintings. How did they manage to collect them?

00:18:28.190 --> 00:18:30.820
Ahh, it's that company of that singer who writes his own songs, isn't it?

00:18:30.820 --> 00:18:32.440
He also had his own sister become an artist...

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:34.000
Ogata Productions?!

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:37.730
What's wrong, Kenichi?

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:43.140
Dad, I think you should stay away from these paintings.

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:47.500
For as long as I could remember, my mother wasn't there for me.

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:51.870
Even now, I still haven't been told whether she's alive or dead.

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:56.120
Our father, who raised us all by himself as a single man, was in a traffic accident.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:19:01.320
Right before he died, he entrusted us to his close friend, Nagase-san.

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:04.740
Since then, he's been taking care of us.

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:07.140
The fact that I was able to attend high school,

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:09.450
and that my brother was able to go overseas,

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:11.300
is all thanks to Nagase-san.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:14.800
I only found out about that recently, too.

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:19.370
It was during November of last year, when I went to Echoes for the first time.

00:19:19.370 --> 00:19:21.310
It was thanks to Yuki.

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:22.980
Yuki... san?

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:26.450
What was originally Nagase-san's listening room,

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:29.610
has also been remodelled as a place for my brother to hide himself.

00:19:29.610 --> 00:19:33.800
Because of this, even though Nagase-san has such a wonderful audio system,

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:37.640
he ended up listening to his music using headphones in a storage closet in the shop.

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:39.090
Poor him.

00:19:41.810 --> 00:19:43.860
And then, at that time...

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:47.120
What is it? All of a sudden...

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:53.090
So he's your Daddy Longlegs. Were you happy, Rina-san?

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:54.470
Yes.

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:56.440
We live in different worlds.

00:19:56.440 --> 00:20:00.660
So different, it makes my head spin.

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:02.720
President, aren't you married?

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.030
I was, and then we divorced.

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:07.110
I'm sorry.

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:13.650
He's the son of a wealthy family that governs one of the largest corporations in the world.

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:17.120
In order to continue the legacy of his father who suddenly passed away,

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:20.930
we were split apart. Us, and our children.

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:22.180
Your children?

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:26.750
Two daughters. The older one is with him, and the younger one is with me.

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:32.180
You know, when she was small, my daughter thought Yuki-chan was really her older sister.

00:20:32.820 --> 00:20:36.000
We lived in the same neighborhood, and so they often played together.

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:37.620
Yuki...

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:38.920
You mean... Yuki?!

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:42.500
She's a distant relative of mine on my mother's side.

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:45.170
For us to meet again in the same industry,

00:20:45.170 --> 00:20:48.640
this is what they call being unable to deny what's in our blood, I suppose.

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:51.410
It doesn't seem like Mana remembers, though.

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:54.360
But that's expected, since I just left her alone all the time.

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:57.280
I'm a terrible mother, aren't I?

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:00.870
I mean, I had no idea...

00:21:00.870 --> 00:21:04.020
... that my daughter's private tutor was actually Touya Fujii.

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:08.930
So Fujii-kun's student... is actually your-!

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:11.800
She passed her university examinations.

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:15.380
Though, no thanks to him. It's because my daughter's brilliant.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:20.850
Yes, all I did was work.

00:21:20.850 --> 00:21:25.620
I believed that making my company bigger was for the sake of everything.

00:21:25.620 --> 00:21:28.890
For my sake, for my divorced husband,

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:31.810
and above all, for my daughter.

00:21:32.010 --> 00:21:34.230
For your husband?

00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:38.260
"M&M" stands for Matsuyama and Mizuki.

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:40.660
We decided on it together when the company was founded.

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:42.420
Matsuyama...

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:43.860
You're very astute.

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:47.280
Menou is my daughter.

00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:51.470
Are you tired?

00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:53.120
This was a great stress-reliever.

00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:55.330
I'm going this way.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:56.790
I see.

00:21:56.790 --> 00:21:57.720
Bye.

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:21.360
Yes.

00:22:21.950 --> 00:22:23.630
Yes, that's right.

00:22:25.220 --> 00:22:27.010
Yes, I understand.

00:22:35.060 --> 00:22:40.020
A Shocking Confession - Magazine Exclusive Matsuyama Menou: I never sang

00:22:49.480 --> 00:22:56.020
watashi ni itsumo anata wa yasashii

00:22:49.480 --> 00:22:56.020
You have always been kind to me

00:22:56.950 --> 00:23:02.590
sono yasashisa ga fuan ni suru

00:22:56.950 --> 00:23:02.590
But this kindness makes me insecure

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:11.430
unmei no ito hodokenai you ni

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:11.430
This string of fate, I'll retie it over and over

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:18.040
nando mo musubi naoshite

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:18.040
So that it will never come loose

00:23:19.240 --> 00:23:26.410
tsugi ni au yakusoku dekinai mama

00:23:19.240 --> 00:23:26.410
I don't want to hear you say goodbye

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:36.360
wakare no kotoba mada kikitaku wa nai yo

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:36.360
Until we make promises to meet again

00:23:36.690 --> 00:23:44.100
aenai yoru ni yume de aetara

00:23:36.690 --> 00:23:44.100
Even if we can't meet tonight, 
if I can see you in my dreams

00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:52.010
ashita ga tsurakute mo waratte irareru

00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:52.010
Even if tomorrow is difficult I'll be able to smile

00:23:52.010 --> 00:23:59.480
donna ni tooku hanarete ite mo

00:23:52.010 --> 00:23:59.480
No matter how far apart we may become

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:09.460
tsunagatte ireru to shinjite iru

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:09.460
I believe that we will still be connected together

00:24:21.900 --> 00:24:24.440
Page 24

00:24:24.440 --> 00:24:26.750
The night will not do anything for us.

00:24:26.750 --> 00:24:29.880
It is because of the sun that the colors fade.

00:24:29.880 --> 00:24:31.410
White Album.
